            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="0312" n="304" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg304"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.20211 Tachibana, Itaru/29: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-11T16:00:00+09:00">July 11, 1941—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 13—9:03 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>984. Department’s 377, July 7, 10 p.m., missionaries in Korea. An official of the
                    Foreign Office informed a member of my staff today that if any of the
                    missionaries declined to leave Korea when the offer is made judicial proceedings
                    would continue and judgment made according to law; that if any were then
                    sentenced the Korean judiciary could hardly be expected to entertain appeals for
                    clemency once having offered to permit them to leave the country.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department via Shanghai.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
